35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I have found some interesting patterns in the old files. It seems the simpler, more foundational projects often leave a longer legacy.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The data on personnel is concerning. There is a significant gap between the skills requested in many proposals and the actual staff available.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"I am worried. The shared instrumentation is failing due to lack of maintenance, and the glasshouses are completely full. We cannot fund a project that requires these.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears the agency is quite generous with computing, but the cost of physical biological maintenance is now shifting heavily onto the awardee.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I am quite worried too. The incident logs show that equipment downtime is a major bottleneck, and biological risks are causing frequent overruns.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Victoria, that is a shame. Perhaps we should look for a candidate whose work is less dependent on those fragile systems.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Benjamin, that aligns with my findings. If the technical staff are gone, the funding for the bench is useless. We need a project that fits the current workforce.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"Exactly. If we fund a high-demand project now, we are setting the researcher up for failure because the infrastructure cannot support them.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"A tragedy of the commons, indeed. We must prioritize a proposal that is computationally heavy but physically lean, given the current subsidies.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,I agree. It would be so sad to see a wonderful project fail just because of a service contract or a full greenhouse. Let's be careful.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I feel we are all reaching a similar conclusion. Let us be kind to the researchers by choosing a project that is actually feasible.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,I will maintain my stance. Reason dictates that we cannot award a grant to a project that lacks the human hands to perform the work.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,I agree. I will support any candidate who does not rely on the overbooked facilities or the failing instrumentation.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,I shall be looking for the candidate who has cleverly shifted their needs toward the centrally funded computing resources.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I just want to make sure the winner can actually spend their time on science, not on fighting with administration or broken machines.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
