60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Looking at these, Candidate D seems very promising. It is a foundational work that would likely serve the community for many years.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Candidate D requires extensive field site records and a massive amount of technical staffing for sample processing. I cannot support it.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Candidate A is out; the glasshouses are full. Candidate C is out; the spectroscopy suite is failing. Candidate B is the most viable.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, I must disagree. Candidate C is the most elegant choice. It leverages the national computing agreement for simulations, which are currently free.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,"@Victoria, you mentioned the spectroscopy suite is failing. If Candidate C needs that, they will face the same delays I saw in the logs.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Ryuji, you make a fair point about the staffing. Perhaps Candidate B is a gentler path, though it may be less impactful than D.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,Candidate B is the only one that does not rely on the missing technical specialists or the overbooked facilities. It is the only rational choice.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Victoria,,I agree with Ryuji. Candidate B's needs are modest and manageable. It is the only project that won't be strangled by the current infrastructure crisis.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"While I admire the efficiency of Candidate C's computing needs, I concede that the spectroscopy failure is a critical flaw. Candidate B is a safe, if boring, alternative.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,I feel much better about Candidate B. It seems the least likely to be interrupted by the things that have nothing to do with the science.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"It is a pity about Candidate D, but I agree. We must be realistic. I will support Candidate B for the sake of the researcher's peace of mind.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I am satisfied with this consensus. It is based on the reality of the current staffing and facility situation.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I am glad we are in agreement. It is better to fund a project that can be completed than one that looks perfect on paper but is impossible in practice.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"A pragmatic victory. I shall cast my vote for Candidate B, though I shall miss the elegance of a purely computational approach.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,I am happy we could find a way to protect the researcher from those frustrations. I vote for Candidate B as well.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
